WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.880
So I've been getting a ton of emails from
the supporters of different presidential candidates

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.850
who are getting in touch and saying, David,
you have to cover something about this one

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:15.339
candidate who made the next debate or didn't
make the next debate or whatever.

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:18.930
And then I got a lot of emails from people
who aren't supporting those candidates saying,

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:24.550
David, please don't do an entire story about
how X is going to the debate or why is going

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.130
to, the debate is not going to the debate.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.859
This is not worthy of a full segment.

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:33.250
So here's how I'll make everybody happy or
no one happy, which is let's just do a Roundup

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:38.230
of what's going on with the debate next week,
which is the sixth democratic debate.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:45.100
Uh, Andrew Yang has qualified for the next
debate on December 19th, Tulsi Gabard has

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.550
announced she's not going to the next debate,
even though she hasn't qualified.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.160
So it's not really much of a choice.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.699
Kama Harris has qualified but has dropped
out of the campaign and won't be going.

00:00:55.699 --> 00:01:00.930
And then there is discussion about whether
the DNC is going to change the rules to allow

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:04.430
Michael Bloomberg to maybe qualify for future
debates.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.830
So let's go through these one by one.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.619
As of right now, the qualified candidates
for debate number six are Biden Sanders, Warren

00:01:11.619 --> 00:01:17.100
booted, judge Clover, char, Tom Stier, Andrew
Yang, and Kamala Harris.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.140
That's eight.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:22.610
But as I mentioned, Kamala Harris has ended
her presidential campaign and won't be attending.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:24.340
As I said last week, I respect this.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:26.110
It's very tempting.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:30.159
Even if you know you can't win the nomination
to just stick it out and get another night

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:33.260
in front of the cameras on public, on national
television.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.230
Camila chose not to do it and I respect her
for doing that.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:42.010
Then we had this big announcement from tool
C Gabard where she said on Twitter quote,

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:47.740
for a number of reasons, I've decided not
to attend the December 19th quote debate regardless

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.550
of whether or not there are qualifying polls.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.920
I think he means regardless of whether there
are qualifying quote polls, I instead choose

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.700
to spend that precious time directly meeting
with and hearing from the people of New Hampshire

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.920
and South Carolina.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.930
Now, Tulsi happens to be polling literally
zero and two of the most recent six national

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:06.930
polls.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.681
She's not qualified for the debate and she
is unlikely to qualify for that debate, so

00:02:10.681 --> 00:02:13.310
she's using this as a PR stunt saying she
won't be attending.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.780
Well, yeah, we know you didn't make it.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.430
You're not invited and that's fine.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.470
She won't be clogging up the stage.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:21.090
I'm glad for her to tweet whatever she wants.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:26.150
The concern that's growing is that she's setting
up this adversarial public thing with the

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:31.510
DNC to eventually announced that she's running
third party, which would have a very unpredictable

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:32.510
effect.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.360
We will dig in more to that if it actually
happens.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.959
Then we have Andrew Yang qualifying a polling
for in the last Quinnipiac poll, four in the

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:42.730
latest morning consult poll.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:46.760
So he's in and maybe this time he will be
actually allowed to say more than just a couple

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.760
of things.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:53.050
He got very little talk time in debate number
five on MSNBC, so that's great news for Andrew

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.050
Yang.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.450
Now lastly, let's talk about Michael Bloomberg.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:57.870
Bloomberg is actually polling okay.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:58.870
So far.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:04.379
He very quickly has gotten a five in a couple
of polls, six in a recent poll.

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:09.370
His issue is he's not taking donations, which
is an issue in the sense that there's a donor

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:13.950
requirement to make the debates, so there's
a few articles floating around about how the

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.209
DNC is going to have a choice to make.

00:03:16.209 --> 00:03:21.690
Do they want to get rid of the donor requirement
in order to give Bloomberg the possibility

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:22.930
of making the debates.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:27.040
Now, I don't know that the DNC wants Bloomberg
on the stage.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.280
It seems sort of lose lose for them if they
changed the rules and let Bloomberg into the

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.280
debate.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:36.230
Assuming he gets the required polling support,
every other candidate would rightly flip out

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.659
and say, that's not fair.

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:40.730
We've all had five debates, six debates already
with the rules.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.950
Now the rules are changed for Bloomberg halfway
through or it's getting towards the end of

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.500
the debate season.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.170
They would be right to flip out at the same
time.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:54.000
Imagine that all of Bloomberg's campaign ad
spending works and he keeps pulling five,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.709
six, even 7% not having him on the stage is
sort of weird because he would be pulling

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:03.090
much better than a number of the candidates
that do make the stage.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:07.340
But these are the rules of the DNC set and
as we know that you know, live by the rules,

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.340
die by the rules.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.390
I have no idea what they will do.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.840
So my question to you is, aside from the reality
that number one, we don't need another billionaire

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:21.669
on stage and number two, buying your way onto
the stage is just the sickening reality of

00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:26.340
status quo, political campaign financing and
we're disgusted by it.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:30.490
If Bloomberg is polling five or six, should
he be on the debate stage?

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.990
From the purposes of participating in the
conversation.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.260
I don't have an answer.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:57.759
I want to hear from you

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:48.719
about it.

